We use the dates from the contract as arguments to the [[create]] command.
Finally, we must ensure to set [[draft]] to [[True]] to not store the contract.

The booking window is the stored [[bookings_start]] and [[bookings_end]]
when the contract has them (\cref{sec:carry-difference}); older
contracts don't, and for them the contract dates are the best we have.
The draft is computed as a replacement of the shown contract: the shown
contract overlaps it, so what it carried is computed afresh rather than
taken as already accounted for.
It reads the courses the contract was created from
([[contract_course_selection]] below), so that the TA's bookings in other
courses don't show up as changes.
Those courses may have left the register since, as courses of past
years do.
[[create]] exits when no course matches, which would end the listing
here, so we check first and skip the draft with a warning instead.
