@

The contract stores the course regex it was created with.
The regex, not the list of courses it matched, is what the user asked
for, so a course added to the register since then that matches it is
read too, just as re-running [[create]] would.
The registers, however, the contract only knows through the courses it
stores, and [[create]] doesn't store its [[--register]] regex.
We therefore read exactly the registers of the stored courses: the names
are escaped, since a register name is not a regex, and anchored at the
end, since [[registers_regex]] anchors only the start
([[re.match]]).
Older contracts lack these fields; for them we fall back to what
[[create]] defaults to, all courses of the default register.
<<helper functions>>=
def contract_course_selection(contract):
  """
  Returns (course_regex, register) selecting the courses that `contract`
  was created from, for re-computing it with the current bookings.
  """
  course_regex = contract.get("course_regex") or ".*"
  if contract.get("courses"):
    registers = sorted({re.escape(register)
                        for _, register in contract["courses"]})
    return course_regex, f"({'|'.join(registers)})$"
  return course_regex, coursescli.MINE
@

The draft must show the same contract with today's bookings, so it must
read the courses the contract was created from, not every course of the
register.
Otherwise the TA's sessions in other courses show up as changes, although
nothing changed for this contract.
Here [[erin]] also works in DD1337, which her contract for DD1310 doesn't
cover: the draft must still come out at the contract's hours.
Her courses are in the register [[reg]], not the default one.
We create her contract with the scenario's stub, which ignores the
register, since [[create]] reads the default register.
Only then do we swap in a stub that selects registers as
[[get_courses_configs]] does, so the draft must find [[reg]] itself.
We drop the scenario's period~1 contract: it stores no courses, so its
own draft would look in the default register only.
<<test functions>>=
def test_show_updates_reads_only_the_contracts_courses(tmp_path,
                                                       monkeypatch):
  import typerconf
  from typer.testing import CliRunner
  from nytid.cli import hr as hrcli
  _erin_scenario(tmp_path, monkeypatch)
  for p1_file in (tmp_path / "contracts").glob("erin.*.json"):
    p1_file.unlink()
  created = CliRunner().invoke(hrcli.cli,
                               ERIN_P2_ALONE + ["--event-summary"])
  hours = f"{_printed_hours(created.stdout):.2f} h"

  scenario_courses = hrcli.coursescli.get_courses_configs
  scenario_sheet = nytid.signup.sheets.read_signup_sheet_from_url
  other = typerconf.Config({"signupsheet": {"url": "https://example.com/t.csv"},
                            "code": "DD1337"})
  other_sheet = [_sheet_row("2025-12-01 10:00", "2025-12-01 14:00",
                            event="DD1337 Laboration")]
  def courses_with_other(regex, register=hrcli.coursescli.MINE):
    courses = scenario_courses("DD1310" if regex == ".*" else regex)
    if regex == ".*":
