\subsection{Reporting}

The [[report]] command is [[missing]] plus persistence: for each
missing TA it prints the identity line that goes to HR and stores the
record.
The weekly cron script captures the printed lines and mails them
(\cref{CLIoverview}), which dictates two design points.

First, there is no plain output form.
The record must snapshot exactly what HR receives, so the identity
lookup is not optional; we fix [[detailed]] to [[True]] instead of
offering an option that could silently store less.
For a quick look without side effects, that is what [[missing]] is
for.

Second, a TA whose identity cannot be resolved is skipped, not
stored.
New TAs regularly aren't in UG and Canvas yet when they first appear
in a sign-up sheet; the old script filtered such bare-username lines
out of the mail so they would be retried the following week.
Skipping the store keeps that retry behaviour, and it also covers a
Canvas or LADOK outage in the cron context: nothing is falsely marked
reported, and the next run heals.

We print each line \emph{before} storing its record.
If the command dies mid-run, the worst case is a TA that was mailed
but not stored, who is then re-reported next week---a duplicate mail,
the same benign failure the old script had.
The opposite order would store without mailing: the TA silently never
reaches HR, which is exactly the failure this feature exists to
prevent.
