\subsection{Ignoring colleagues}

Colleagues who sign up on the course must not be reported to HR as
TAs, and external examiners may be employed elsewhere.
Previously this was handled by [[nytid-ignore.sh]] appending lines to
a file that the weekly script never read (\cref{CLIoverview}); now an ignore
is just an employment record with [[ignored]] set, stored in the same
place the coverage check reads.

The user regex has no default: ignoring is deliberate, and
defaulting to everyone would be a destructive typo away.
We resolve the regex against the TAs actually booked on the matching
courses, so a typo matches no one instead of storing a useless
record, and we echo each ignored username so the caller sees exactly
who matched.
Unlike [[report]], we skip the identity lookup: the record only needs
to suppress reporting, and an external colleague may not resolve in
Canvas at all.
For the same reason the config-derived expiry does not apply---a
colleague is not reset over summer---so an ignore lasts until
explicitly given a [[--valid-until]] or deleted.
