\subsection{The booked hours}

For each TA booked in the period, [[booked_hourly_hours]] gives the
username, the personnummer and the name, which Medvind identifies the
TA by, and the booked salary hours.
The personnummer and the name come from LADOK, as for the time sheets
(\cref{WorkingWithTimesheets}).
Without LADOK there is no personnummer, and we fall back on the name
Canvas has, which is what Medvind shows unless the TA goes by another
name in one of them.
Without Canvas either, all we have is the username, which matches no
name in Medvind.
A TA we cannot find comes out twice, once with all the booked hours
missing and once as an unbooked reporter, so the mail shows the two
halves side by side rather than hiding them.

An amanuensis gets [[None]] as hours rather than being left out.
We still need the personnummer: their times in Medvind are theirs and
must not turn up as times reported by someone we have no bookings for.

Whether a TA is an amanuensis we decide as the time sheets do
(\cref{sec:timesheets-amanuensis}): by whether a contract employs them
on the day of their last session.
The two must agree, since the TAs report in Medvind what the time sheet
drafts tell them.

The decision is for the whole TA, here too.
A TA whose contract ends mid-month and who works hourly after it is not
compared that month.
That is rare, and comparing an amanuensis's sessions as if they were to
be reported would flood the mail every month instead.
<<helper functions>>=
def booked_hourly_hours(courses, course_regex, start, end):
  """
  Returns `(user, personnummer, name, hours)` for each TA booked in
  `courses` from `start` to `end` (dates, inclusive). `hours` is the
  booked salary hours, prep time included, or None for an amanuensis.
  `personnummer` is None when LADOK can't give it.
  """
  <<signup machinery imports>>
  <<let [[booked]] be all bookings from [[courses]]>>
  booked = sheets.filter_events_by_date(
    booked,
    datetime.datetime.combine(start, datetime.time.min),
    datetime.datetime.combine(end, datetime.time.max))

  tas = []
  for user in sorted(hr.hours_per_TA(booked)):
    <<set [[user_obj]] to most detailed version possible of [[user]]>>
    try:
      personnummer = user_obj.personnummer
      name = f"{user_obj.first_name} {user_obj.last_name}"
    except AttributeError as err:
      logging.warning(f"can't access {user}'s LADOK data: {err}")
      personnummer = None
      name = getattr(user_obj, "name", user)

    events = summarize_user(user, booked)
    first, last = sessions_span(events)
    if employed_on(user, last):
      hours = None
    else:
      hours = sum(event["omr_tid"] for event in events)
    tas.append((user, personnummer, name, hours))
  return tas
@

The whole of [[booked_hourly_hours]] runs on real sign-up rows and the
real contracts of [[temp_contracts_dir]].
What we replace is what the test cannot reach: the download of the
sheet, and Canvas and LADOK, which only Alice is in.
Erin has two two-hour labs, one in September and one in October; with
the hourly prep factor of 1.8 for labs (\cref{HRaddprep}), rounded up
to a quarter (\cref{HRroundtime}), the September one counts 3.75 hours.
Alice's lab is covered by her contract, and so is her lab in
October: it is after the last session of her contract but within her
employment.
Bob's first lab in October is before his employment starts on the
27th, his second after; the last decides, so he is not compared.
Erin has no contract and is compared in both months.
