\subsection{Testing the command}

The command test runs the real command through [[nytid]]'s top-level
app, against the local Medvind server of the library's tests with its
recorded answers, as the tests of the other Medvind commands do
(\cref{cli.medvind.tests}).
The bookings are the part we replace: they come from Google Sheets,
Canvas and LADOK, which the test cannot reach, and
[[booked_hourly_hours]] only combines helpers that are tested
elsewhere in this chapter.
So we monkeypatch it to two booked hourly TAs, Tolvan and Tolva.
Tolva's times have no work leader, so under Ada Lärare she has reported
nothing.
<<test setup>>=
@pytest.fixture
def medvind_server(monkeypatch):
  import requests
  import nytid.medvind
  with local_server(medvind_routes()) as (url, received):
    monkeypatch.setattr(nytid.medvind, "BASE_URL", url)
    monkeypatch.setattr(nytid.medvind, "shared_session", requests.Session)
    yield received
<<test functions>>=
def test_cli_medvind_deviations(medvind_server, monkeypatch):
  from typer.testing import CliRunner
  from nytid.cli import cli as nytid_cli
  from nytid.cli import hr as hrcli

  monkeypatch.setattr(hrcli.coursescli, "get_courses_configs",
                      lambda *args, **kwargs: {("DD1301", "mine"): None})
  monkeypatch.setattr(hrcli, "booked_hourly_hours",
                      lambda *args: [(*TOLVAN, 6.5),
                                     ("tolva", "121212-2223",
                                      "Tolva Tolvansson", 2)])

  def deviations(*options):
    result = CliRunner().invoke(nytid_cli, [
      "hr", "medvind", "deviations", "DD1301",
      "--from", "2026-06-01", "--to", "2026-09-30", *options])
    assert result.exit_code == 0, result.output
    return result.stdout.splitlines()

  assert deviations("--leader", "Ada") == [
    "tolva\tTolva Tolvansson\t2\t0\t-2"]
  assert deviations("--leader", "Nobody") == [
    "tolvan\tTolvan Tolvansson\t6.5\t0\t-6.5",
    "tolva\tTolva Tolvansson\t2\t0\t-2"]
@

Without a work leader the command cannot know which times are ours, so
it refuses, naming the configuration key.
The test suite runs with an empty configuration
(\cref{sec:isolating-the-config}), so leaving out [[--leader]] is
enough:
<<test functions>>=
def test_cli_medvind_deviations_needs_a_leader(caplog):
  from typer.testing import CliRunner
  from nytid.cli import cli as nytid_cli

  result = CliRunner().invoke(nytid_cli,
                              ["hr", "medvind", "deviations", "DD1301"])
  assert result.exit_code == 1
  assert "medvind.leader" in caplog.text
